From: xe3000-open-firmware <noreply@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] bus: mhi: pci_generic: add explicit entry for 17cb:0308 sub 17cb:5201

The GL-XE3000 modem enumerates as PCI 17cb:0308 with subsystem 17cb:5201.
Add an explicit subsystem match ahead of the generic 17cb:0308 fallback so
this board can later get its own mhi_pci_dev_info without disturbing other
SDX65 based modules. Behaviour is unchanged for now (same sdx65 info).

NOT VERIFIED on hardware: the IDs come from the project notes, the choice
of mhi_qcom_sdx65_info is an assumption until the stock firmware analysis
confirms the channel layout.

Signed-off-by: xe3000-open-firmware <noreply@example.invalid>
---
--- a/drivers/bus/mhi/host/pci_generic.c
+++ b/drivers/bus/mhi/host/pci_generic.c
@@ -738,6 +738,9 @@ static const struct pci_device_id mhi_pci_id_table[] = {
 	/* Telit FE990A */
 	{ PCI_DEVICE_SUB(PCI_VENDOR_ID_QCOM, 0x0308, 0x1c5d, 0x2015),
 		.driver_data = (kernel_ulong_t) &mhi_telit_fe990a_info },
+	/* GL.iNet XE3000 modem: explicit subsystem entry so the board can get its own mhi_pci_dev_info later */
+	{ PCI_DEVICE_SUB(PCI_VENDOR_ID_QCOM, 0x0308, PCI_VENDOR_ID_QCOM, 0x5201),
+		.driver_data = (kernel_ulong_t) &mhi_qcom_sdx65_info },
 	{ PCI_DEVICE(PCI_VENDOR_ID_QCOM, 0x0308),
 		.driver_data = (kernel_ulong_t) &mhi_qcom_sdx65_info },
 	{ PCI_DEVICE(PCI_VENDOR_ID_QCOM, 0x0309),
